Key provisions include:

Criminal Offenses & Penalties:
Defines modern slavery offenses, including forced labor, human trafficking, and exploitation.
Life imprisonment for offenders convicted of slavery or human trafficking.
Victim Protection & Support:
Independent Anti-Slavery Commissioner to improve victim support.
Increased protections for children and vulnerable individuals.
Corporate Transparency & Supply Chains:
Companies with an annual turnover of £36 million+ must publish a Modern Slavery Statement.
The statement must detail actions taken to prevent slavery in supply chains.
Failure to report can lead to civil penalties and reputational risks.
Asset Confiscation & Reparation Orders:
Courts can confiscate assets of convicted individuals.
Victims can receive compensation from seized assets.
The Act aligns with international human rights and labor standards, reinforcing the UK’s commitment to ending modern slavery.', 'The Modern Slavery Act 2015 establishes legal frameworks to combat slavery, servitude, forced labor, and human trafficking. It enhances victim protection, strengthens law enforcement measures, and introduces corporate transparency requirements.

